a 300-line paste says 300 lines

§6: *"the truthful paste line count where you report 301 lines for a 300-line paste"*.

The count was `s.matches('\n').count() + 1`. That is right for text with no final
newline and wrong for text with one, and **almost every real paste has one**: a file
dragged out of an editor ends `…\n`, a stack trace copied out of a terminal ends in a
newline, a `git diff` ends in one. So the number the composer shows was one larger than
the number of lines it stood for.

`lines()` is the count a reader would make: `"a\nb\n"` and `"a\nb"` are both two lines,
and an empty paste is zero — which is below the threshold and therefore not collapsed,
which is the right answer for a paste of nothing.

## The same off-by-one from the other side, and it is the half that changes behaviour

The count and the threshold read the same string, so a paste of **four lines ending in a
newline** used to count five and collapse, while the same four lines without the final
newline did not. Two pastes that are the same four lines behaved differently on a
difference nobody can see — which is the honest reason this is not merely a wrong label.
Both directions are pinned now.

## Tests

- `the_paste_count_is_the_lines_a_reader_would_count` — 300 lines with and without the
  final newline both read `~300 lines`; four lines stay ordinary typed text and five
  collapse.
- `a_large_paste_becomes_a_placeholder_and_expands_on_submit` asserted `~41 lines` for a
  40-line fixture, which was the defect written down as the expectation. It says `~40`
  now, and that edit is the point rather than a chore: **a test that encodes the bug is a
  test that would fail on the fix**, which is worth noticing when the fix is this small.

`cargo test -p letibot-ui`: **102 passed, 0 failed** (101 + 1).
`cargo test -p letibot-tui`: **312 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored**.

**Not verified, and said rather than glossed:** `rustfmt --check` cannot run — it writes a
temp file and `bash` is closed for that direction by the circuit breaker, which only the
operator lifts. The four crate suites outside these two are still unrun since `65725ce`,
for the lock reasons the last four commits record.

## Not in this commit

The rest of §6's list, one item per commit: `/todos`, `/subagents`, `/peek`, `/resume`,
`/promote`, `q` closing any pane, `ctrl-o` into a subagent, clicks reaching five panes
instead of two, SGR mouse motion decoded, the composer draft preserved across a history
walk, and the tail-origin scroll sign for the peek and job-output panes.
